---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---
<Page title="Privacy Policy: Analytics, AdSense Cookies and Your Choices" description="How Daily Crypto News uses Google Analytics 4 and AdSense, which cookies may be set, consent in the EEA, UK and Switzerland, and how to opt out of personal ads." path="/privacy/" h1="What data does Daily Crypto News collect?" mark="Privacy" updated="2026-10-15"
  answer="We do not run accounts or collect forms. Google Analytics 4 measures visits and Google AdSense shows ads; both may use cookies. Visitors in the EEA, UK and Switzerland are asked for consent first, and anyone can opt out of personalised ads.">
  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>Daily Crypto News ({site.domain}) is the controller for this website. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No accounts or forms.</strong> The calculators run in your browser; inputs are not sent to us.</li>
    <li><strong>Server logs.</strong> Our static host (Cloudflare) processes IP addresses and request data to deliver pages and protect against abuse.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics.</strong> When enabled, Google Analytics 4 records pages viewed, approximate location, device type and events such as using a tool. IP addresses are not logged or stored by GA4.</li>
    <li><strong>Email.</strong> If you write to us, we keep the message to reply and for our records.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Advertising and third-party cookies</h2>
  <p>We use Google AdSense. Google and its partners use cookies or similar identifiers to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and other websites, to limit repeat ads, and to measure performance. Third-party vendors, including Google, may place and read cookies on your browser.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Learn how Google uses data: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</li>
    <li>Opt out of personalised advertising: <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/">Google Ads Settings</a>, or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/">aboutads.info</a> for other vendors.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Consent in the EEA, UK and Switzerland</h2>
  <p>For visitors in these regions, analytics and advertising storage default to <em>denied</em> using Google Consent Mode, and consent is collected through Google’s certified consent management platform before personalised ads or analytics cookies are used. You can change your choice at any time through the consent link shown by the platform.</p>
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live you may have rights to access, correct, delete or object to processing of personal data. Email us and we will respond within the time required by applicable law. You can also block cookies in your browser settings.</p>
  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>GA4 data is kept for the retention period configured in our Google Analytics property (no longer than 14 months). Emails are deleted when no longer needed.</p>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We will update this page and its date when practices change. See also the <a href="/terms/">terms</a> and <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.</p>
</Page>
